{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_mmdfqr6i45unvj9w7b","content":"# Planning Log: Hankweave Monorepo Migration\n\n## Areas Read\n\n- [x] source/hankweave/server - core runtime code (60+ .ts files, well-organized subdirs)\n- [x] source/hankweave/package.json - @southbridgeai/hankweave v0.5.6, Bun runtime, many scripts\n- [x] source/hankweave/scripts/ - build.ts, build-executable.ts, release.ts, sync-public.ts, generate-schemas.ts, e2e/init.ts, run-cross-runtime-tests.ts, test-sync-local.ts\n- [x] source/hankweave/.github/workflows/ - ci.yml, release.yml, sync-public.yml\n- [x] source/hankweave/.github/actions/ - setup-environment, run-tests, dump-test-logs (composite actions)\n- [x] source/hankweave/biome.json - covers server/, tests/e2e/, tests/utils/, tests/unit/, types/\n- [x] source/hankweave/bunfig.toml - minimal, just BUN_TEST env var for tests\n- [x] source/hankweave/tsconfig.json - ES2022, strict, bun-types\n- [x] source/hankweave/.gitignore, .npmignore, .gitattributes\n- [x] source/hankweave/standard-operating-procedures.md - comprehensive SOPs\n- [x] source/hankweave-docs/ - Nextra 4, Next.js 15, Bun install+build\n- [x] source/hankweave-docs/nextra-site/package.json - hankweave-docs v2.0.0\n- [x] source/hankweave-docs/nextra-site/vercel.json - framework: nextjs, bun install/build\n- [x] source/hankweave-docs/nextra-site/tsconfig.json - ES2020, strict:false, bundler resolution\n- [x] source/hankweave/tests/ - 65+ unit tests, 10+ integration, 10+ e2e, cross-runtime tests\n- [x] plan/background/background.md - pre-compiled research\n\n## Aha Moments\n\n### 1. The docs project has a nested structure\nThe docs repo is `hankweave-docs/` at root but the actual Next.js project is at `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/`. The `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, `next.config.mjs` etc. are all inside `nextra-site/`. The docs repo root has `README.md`, `.gitignore`, `notes/`, `plan/`.\n\nThis means that wherever docs lands in the monorepo, you need to decide: does the workspace point to the `nextra-site/` subdirectory (where package.json lives), or to the outer `hankweave-docs/` directory?\n\n**Decision**: The workspace should point to where `package.json` is — so the `nextra-site/` level. The outer `hankweave-docs/` scaffold (README, notes, plan) is development overhead that probably doesn't need its own workspace and can either be flattened or kept as-is.\n\n### 2. generate-schemas.ts is the only real cross-repo code reference\nGrep confirms only `scripts/generate-schemas.ts:28` references `hankweave-docs` in actual code. All other references are in `intermediates/` planning documents (which are stripped on release). This simplifies the migration — only one file needs a path adjustment.\n\n### 3. The docs have NO dependency on the runtime package\nThe docs site (`hankweave-docs`) doesn't `import` anything from `@southbridgeai/hankweave`. The only cross-repo data flow is schemas generated by the runtime and written to the docs `public/schemas/` directory. A `workspace:*` dependency is NOT needed at this time.\n\n### 4. The public sync pipeline only needs to export the runtime\nThe `sync-public.ts` script works from the root of the hankweave repo. In a monorepo, if the runtime stays at the root, the sync script barely changes. If it moves into a subdirectory, the strip lists and snapshot process need reworking.\n\n### 5. CI uses composite actions with relative paths\nAll three composite actions (`.github/actions/*`) are referenced as `./.github/actions/setup-environment` etc. These use relative paths. As long as the `.github/` directory stays at the monorepo root, they work. The composite actions themselves just do `bun install --frozen-lockfile` and `bun test` — they'd work with workspaces too.\n\n### 6. The release script assumes it runs from the repo root\n`release.ts` uses `resolve(process.cwd())` for paths and runs `git` commands. It also runs `bun run generate-schemas` and `bun run tc`. These all assume the cwd is the package root. In a monorepo with the runtime as a workspace, scripts would need to be run from the workspace directory or paths adjusted.\n\n### 7. build.ts uses relative paths from import.meta.dir\n`build.ts` resolves `distDir` as `join(import.meta.dir, \"..\", \"dist\")` and entry point as `\"./server/index.ts\"`. This means build.ts must run from (or be relative to) the runtime package root. Same for `build-executable.ts`.\n\n### 8. Vercel monorepo support just needs \"Root Directory\"\nVercel lets you set the \"Root Directory\" for a project in project settings. The current `vercel.json` in `nextra-site/` would work if Vercel is pointed at the right subdirectory. This is a settings change, not a code change.\n\n### 9. The docs package.json has a `postbuild` step\n`\"postbuild\": \"pagefind --site .next/server/app --output-path public/_pagefind\"` — this runs Pagefind after `next build`. This would work fine in a workspace since `next build` runs from the workspace directory.\n\n### 10. tsconfig.json settings differ significantly between the two projects\n- Runtime: `target: ES2022`, `module: ES2022`, `moduleResolution: node`, `strict: true`, types: `bun-types`\n- Docs: `target: ES2020`, `module: esnext`, `moduleResolution: bundler`, `strict: false`, plugins: `next`\n\nThese configs should NOT be shared. Each workspace needs its own `tsconfig.json`.\n\n### 11. There's only one bun.lock file per project\nCurrently `source/hankweave/bun.lock` and `source/hankweave-docs/nextra-site/bun.lock`. In a monorepo, there would be a single root-level `bun.lock` file managed by Bun workspaces.\n\n### 12. The runtime's `.npmignore` strips `server/`, `scripts/`, `tests/` for npm publish\nnpm publish only includes `dist/`, `shims/`, `schemas/`. This is controlled by both `.npmignore` and the `\"files\"` field in `package.json`. In a monorepo, the npm publish command would need to run from the runtime workspace. `\"files\"` field should continue to work correctly.\n\n## Key Decision Points\n\n### Structure Decision: Runtime at root vs in a subdirectory\n\n**Option A: Runtime stays at repo root, docs moves in as a workspace**\n```\nhankweave/                  (monorepo root = runtime package root)\n├── package.json            (root package.json with workspaces field, ALSO the runtime)\n├── server/\n├── scripts/\n├── tests/\n├── docs/                   (was: hankweave-docs/nextra-site)\n│   ├── package.json\n│   ├── app/\n│   ├── content/\n│   └── ...\n└── ...\n```\n- Pro: Minimal disruption to existing paths, scripts, CI\n- Pro: All existing relative paths in server/scripts still work\n- Con: The root package.json serves dual purpose (workspace root AND runtime package)\n- Con: `bun install` at root installs both workspace deps — might be slightly confusing\n\n**Option B: Both packages in subdirectories**\n```\nhankweave/                  (monorepo root)\n├── package.json            (workspace root, not a package itself)\n├── packages/\n│   ├── runtime/            (was: hankweave root)\n│   │   ├── package.json\n│   │   ├── server/\n│   │   └── ...\n│   └── docs/               (was: hankweave-docs/nextra-site)\n│       ├── package.json\n│       └── ...\n└── .github/\n```\n- Pro: Clean separation, conventional monorepo structure\n- Con: MASSIVE amount of path changes — every script, CI workflow, build config, `import.meta.dir` reference\n- Con: git history gets complicated\n- Con: The release.ts, sync-public.ts, build.ts all need significant reworking\n\n**Option C: Runtime at root, docs as apps/docs**\n```\nhankweave/                  (monorepo root = runtime package root)\n├── package.json            (root + runtime)\n├── server/\n├── apps/\n│   └── docs/               (was: hankweave-docs/nextra-site)\n│       ├── package.json\n│       └── ...\n└── ...\n```\n- Pro: Distinguishes \"apps\" (deployable) from packages (publishable) — common Turborepo pattern\n- Con: `apps/` is a Turborepo convention that might be overengineering for two packages\n- Otherwise similar to Option A\n\n### Recommendation: Option A (runtime at root)\n\nThe path of least disruption. The runtime is the primary package — it has the most scripts, CI workflows, and tooling built around its position at root. Moving it into a subdirectory would require changing dozens of paths across scripts, workflows, and configs.\n\nThe docs site is the smaller, simpler addition. Putting it at `docs/` (or `docs/nextra-site/`) within the runtime's repo structure is the minimal change.\n\nThe trade-off: the root `package.json` serves double duty. But Bun workspaces handles this fine — you can have `\"workspaces\": [\"docs\"]` in the root and the root itself is also a package.\n\n### Sync-public impact\n\nWith Option A (runtime at root), the sync-public.ts barely changes. The only new item is that the `docs/` directory needs to be added to the `STRIP_DIRS` list so it doesn't end up in the public runtime snapshot. Everything else stays the same.\n\n### CI impact\n\nWith Option A:\n- `ci.yml` barely changes — the runtime is still at root, `bun install` installs all workspaces, tests run from root\n- `release.yml` same thing\n- Optional: Add path filtering so docs-only changes skip runtime tests (nice to have, not required initially)\n\n### generate-schemas.ts impact\n\nThe `DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR` path changes from `../../hankweave-docs/nextra-site/public/schemas` to `../docs/public/schemas` (one level up from `scripts/`, then into `docs/`). This is actually simpler.\n\n## Questions Resolved\n\n1. **Full directory structure** — mapped exhaustively\n2. **Script invocation** — all via `bun run <script>` or `bun scripts/<file>.ts`\n3. **Sync-public strips** — STRIP_DIRS + STRIP_FILES documented, understood\n4. **Test infrastructure** — bun:test, 65+ unit, 10+ integration, e2e with mock LLMs\n5. **server/ depth** — 3-4 levels (server/sentinels/, server/llm/, server/types/, etc.)\n6. **Docs structure** — Nextra 4 + Next.js 15, content/ for MDX, app/ for routes, components/ for custom\n\n## Questions Remaining\n\n1. **Should the outer hankweave-docs/ wrapper be kept?** — The docs repo has a root-level README, notes/, plan/ directory outside nextra-site/. These are dev-only files. Probably flatten: just bring nextra-site/ contents into docs/.\n2. **Shared dev dependencies?** — Both projects use TypeScript. The docs use `@types/node` and `@types/react`. The runtime uses `@types/bun`. Bun catalogs could share TypeScript version, but it's not critical.\n3. **Does the monorepo need its own README at root?** — The current runtime README is internal. The public one is in `public-release-files/`. Adding a monorepo root README could be helpful but isn't strictly necessary for the migration.\n"}]},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:28:32.910Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_mmdfqvfhoi756yi4bx","content":"archive-manifest.ts\nbase-process-manager.ts\nbasic-tui.ts\nbuild-constants.d.ts\ncheckpoint-git.ts\nclaude-agent-sdk-manager.ts\nclaude-log-parser.ts\nclaude-runtime-extractor.ts\ncleanup-command.ts\ncli-parser.ts\ncodex-runtime-extractor.ts\ncodon-runner.ts\ncommand-schemas.ts\nconfig-validation\nconfig.ts\ncost-tracker.ts\ndata-hasher.ts\nevent-journal.ts\nexecution-planner.ts\nexecution-setup.ts\nexecution-thread.ts\nfile-resolver.ts\nhankweave-runtime.ts\nindex.ts\ninit-command.ts\nllm\nllm-proxy.ts\nprompt-builder.ts\nprompt-frontmatter.ts\nremote-hank.ts\nreplay-process-manager.ts\nreplay.ts\nruntime-extractor-base.ts\nschemas\nsentinels\nshim-process-manager.ts\nshim-runtime-extractor.ts\nstate-manager.ts\nstate-transition-guards.ts\nstorage\ntelemetry\ntyped-event-emitter.ts\ntypes\nutils.ts\nvalidate-ascii.ts\nvalidate-command.ts\nwebsocket-log-reader.ts\nwizard\n"}]},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:28:32.911Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_mmdfqz6zp97im71ape","content":"     1\t#!/usr/bin/env bun\n     2\timport crypto from \"node:crypto\";\n     3\timport fs from \"node:fs\";\n     4\timport os from \"node:os\";\n     5\timport path from \"node:path\";\n     6\timport { BasicTUI } from \"./basic-tui.js\";\n     7\timport { ClaudeAgentSDKManager } from \"./claude-agent-sdk-manager.js\";\n     8\timport { CleanupCommand } from \"./cleanup-command.js\";\n     9\timport { parseCliArgs, showDeprecationWarnings } from \"./cli-parser.js\";\n    10\timport { ensureSchemaUrl, resolveSettings, validateHank } from \"./config.js\";\n    11\timport type { ExecutionSetup } from \"./execution-setup.js\";\n    12\timport { setupExecutionEnvironment } from \"./execution-setup.js\";\n    13\timport { HankweaveRuntime } from \"./hankweave-runtime.js\";\n    14\timport { initProject } from \"./init-command.js\";\n    15\timport { LlmProviderRegistry } from \"./llm/llm-provider-registry.js\";\n    16\timport {\n    17\t  displayHankSummary,\n    18\t  getHankSummary,\n    19\t  isRemoteHankUrl,\n    20\t  resolveRemoteHank,\n    21\t} from \"./remote-hank.js\";\n    22\timport {\n    23\t  getOrCreateClientId,\n    24\t  resolveTelemetryConfig,\n    25\t  showFirstRunNotice,\n    26\t  TelemetryCollector,\n    27\t  type TelemetryEventName,\n    28\t} from \"./telemetry/index.js\";\n    29\timport {\n    30\t  getMetadata,\n    31\t  Logger,\n    32\t  renderStartupBanner,\n    33\t  renderStartupInfo,\n    34\t  type StartupInfo,\n    35\t} from \"./utils.js\";\n    36\timport { renderHankStructure } from \"./validate-ascii.js\";\n    37\timport { runValidation } from \"./validate-command.js\";\n    38\timport { runWelcomeWizard } from \"./wizard/welcome-wizard.js\";\n    39\t\n    40\t// -------------\n    41\t// Helper Functions\n    42\t// -------------\n    43\t\n    44\t/**\n    45\t * Fire-and-forget CLI telemetry event.\n    46\t * Used in early-exit paths (--init, --validate, --cleanup, --help)\n    47\t * where the full telemetry system isn't initialized.\n    48\t *\n    49\t * Reads hankweave.json from cwd to respect file-level telemetry opt-out,\n    50\t * matching the behavior of the full runtime path.\n    51\t */\n    52\tasync function sendCliTelemetry(\n    53\t  event: TelemetryEventName,\n    54\t  properties: Record<string, unknown>,\n    55\t): Promise<void> {\n    56\t  try {\n    57\t    // Read telemetry config from hankweave.json if present (same as full runtime path)\n    58\t    let fileTelemetryConfig: Parameters<typeof resolveTelemetryConfig>[0];\n    59\t    try {\n    60\t      const runtimeConfigPath = path.join(process.cwd(), \"hankweave.json\");\n    61\t      if (fs.existsSync(runtimeConfigPath)) {\n    62\t        const raw = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(runtimeConfigPath, \"utf-8\"));\n    63\t        fileTelemetryConfig = raw?.telemetry;\n    64\t      }\n    65\t    } catch {\n    66\t      // Silent fail - config is optional\n    67\t    }\n    68\t\n    69\t    const telemetryConfig = resolveTelemetryConfig(fileTelemetryConfig);\n    70\t    if (!telemetryConfig.enabled) return;\n    71\t    const clientId = await getOrCreateClientId();\n    72\t    const collector = new TelemetryCollector(telemetryConfig, clientId, false);\n    73\t    await collector.trackCliEvent(event, properties);\n    74\t    await collector.shutdown();\n    75\t  } catch {\n    76\t    // Silent fail - CLI telemetry should never block\n    77\t  }\n    78\t}\n    79\t\n    80\t/**\n    81\t * Read content from stdin.\n    82\t * Throws if stdin is a TTY (no piped input).\n    83\t */\n    84\tasync function readStdin(): Promise<string> {\n    85\t  if (process.stdin.isTTY) {\n    86\t    throw new Error('No input provided on stdin. Use: echo \"text\" | hankweave hank.json -');\n    87\t  }\n    88\t\n    89\t  const chunks: Buffer[] = [];\n    90\t  for await (const chunk of process.stdin) {\n    91\t    chunks.push(chunk as Buffer);\n    92\t  }\n    93\t  return Buffer.concat(chunks).toString(\"utf-8\");\n    94\t}\n    95\t\n    96\t/**\n    97\t * Get a stable, content-based file path for inline/stdin input.\n    98\t * This ensures the same input content produces the same data hash across runs,\n    99\t * enabling proper resume functionality with --execution.\n   100\t *\n   101\t * The path is deterministic based on content hash, stored in ~/.hankweave-cache/inputs/\n   102\t * to persist across runs. If the file already exists, we reuse it (preserving mtime)\n   103\t * which keeps the data hash stable.\n   104\t */\n   105\tasync function getStableInputPath(content: string, type: \"input\" | \"stdin\"): Promise<string> {\n   106\t  const contentHash = crypto.createHash(\"sha256\").update(content).digest(\"hex\").slice(0, 16);\n   107\t  const cacheDir = path.join(os.homedir(), \".hankweave-cache\", \"inputs\");\n   108\t\n   109\t  // Ensure cache directory exists\n   110\t  await fs.promises.mkdir(cacheDir, { recursive: true });\n   111\t\n   112\t  const filePath = path.join(cacheDir, `${type}-${contentHash}.txt`);\n   113\t\n   114\t  // Only write if file doesn't exist (preserves mtime for stable hashing)\n   115\t  if (!fs.existsSync(filePath)) {\n   116\t    await fs.promises.writeFile(filePath, content);\n   117\t  }\n   118\t\n   119\t  return filePath;\n   120\t}\n   121\t\n   122\t// -------------\n   123\t// Main Entry Point\n   124\t// -------------\n   125\t\n   126\tasync function main() {\n   127\t  const args = process.argv.slice(2);\n   128\t\n   129\t  // Parse ALL CLI arguments in one place (with validation)\n   130\t  let cliArgs: ReturnType<typeof parseCliArgs>;\n   131\t  try {\n   132\t    cliArgs = parseCliArgs(args);\n   133\t  } catch (error) {\n   134\t    console.error(`Error: ${(error as Error).message}`);\n   135\t    process.exit(1);\n   136\t  }\n   137\t\n   138\t  // Handle version flag - print version and exit\n   139\t  if (cliArgs.showVersion) {\n   140\t    console.log(getMetadata().version);\n   141\t    process.exit(0);\n   142\t  }\n   143\t\n   144\t  // Show deprecation warnings for old flags (before any other output)\n   145\t  showDeprecationWarnings(cliArgs);\n   146\t\n   147\t  // ========== WELCOME WIZARD ==========\n   148\t  // Detect \"bare bones\" invocation: no args, no flags.\n   149\t  // This is the \"I just heard about this and want to try it\" entry point.\n   150\t  const isBareBones =\n   151\t    !cliArgs.hankPath &&\n   152\t    !cliArgs.configPath &&\n   153\t    !cliArgs.dataPath &&\n   154\t    !cliArgs.dataFlag &&\n   155\t    !cliArgs.executionPath &&\n   156\t    !cliArgs.inputText &&\n   157\t    !cliArgs.init &&\n   158\t    !cliArgs.help &&\n   159\t    !cliArgs.showVersion &&\n   160\t    !cliArgs.validate &&\n   161\t    !cliArgs.cleanup &&\n   162\t    !cliArgs.attach &&\n   163\t    !cliArgs.headless &&\n   164\t    !cliArgs.replayDir;\n   165\t\n   166\t  if (isBareBones) {\n   167\t    try {\n   168\t      await runWelcomeWizard();\n   169\t      await sendCliTelemetry(\"cli_init\", { source: \"wizard\" });\n   170\t    } catch (error) {\n   171\t      // If the wizard fails for any reason, don't crash - fall through to normal help\n   172\t      console.error(`\\nWizard error: ${(error as Error).message}\\n`);\n   173\t    }\n   174\t    process.exit(0);\n   175\t  }\n   176\t\n   177\t  // Print startup banner\n   178\t  renderStartupBanner();\n   179\t\n   180\t  // Extract values with defaults\n   181\t  // Note: configPath is resolved later with directory-aware logic\n   182\t  const dataSourcePath = cliArgs.dataPath || cliArgs.dataFlag;\n   183\t  let executionPath = cliArgs.executionPath;\n   184\t  const inlineInput = cliArgs.inputText;\n   185\t  const outputPath = cliArgs.outputPath; // --output flag\n   186\t\n   187\t  const useSymlink = !cliArgs.copy;\n   188\t  const headlessMode = cliArgs.headless || false;\n   189\t  const validateMode = cliArgs.validate || false;\n   190\t  const cleanupMode = cliArgs.cleanup || false;\n   191\t  const skipConfirmation = cliArgs.skipConfirmation || false;\n   192\t  const startNew = cliArgs.startNew || false;\n   193\t  const forceMode = cliArgs.force || false;\n   194\t  const initMode = cliArgs.init || false;\n   195\t  // --ignore-data-mismatch is deprecated, --force now handles this too\n   196\t  const ignoreDataMismatch = cliArgs.ignoreDataMismatch || false;\n   197\t\n   198\t  if (cliArgs.help) {\n   199\t    console.log(`\n   200\tHankweave Runtime - Codon Orchestration\n"}]},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:28:32.911Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_mmdfr3pbrayz0fvh19","content":"     1\timport fs from \"node:fs\";\n     2\timport os from \"node:os\";\n     3\timport path from \"node:path\";\n     4\timport { z } from \"zod\";\n     5\timport { validateModel } from \"./config-validation/model-validator.js\";\n     6\timport { codonSentinelEntrySchema } from \"./config-validation/sentinel.schema.js\";\n     7\timport { LlmProviderRegistry } from \"./llm/llm-provider-registry.js\";\n     8\timport type { ModelInfo } from \"./llm/models-dev-schema.js\";\n     9\timport { type TelemetryConfig, telemetryConfigSchema } from \"./telemetry/telemetry-types.js\";\n    10\timport { CodonId } from \"./types/branded-types.js\";\n    11\timport type { ModelName, ShimSelfTestResult } from \"./types/types.js\";\n    12\timport { deepMerge, getMetadata, type Logger, rmSyncWithRetry } from \"./utils.js\";\n    13\t\n    14\t// Get version from package metadata\n    15\tconst PACKAGE_VERSION = getMetadata().version;\n    16\t\n    17\t// -------------\n    18\t// Constants\n    19\t// -------------\n    20\t\n    21\texport const TIMEOUTS = {\n    22\t  RESULT_MESSAGE_MS: 30000, // 30 seconds to wait for result message\n    23\t  PROCESS_KILL_GRACE_MS: 5000, // 5 seconds grace period before SIGKILL\n    24\t  LOG_PARSER_DELAY_MS: 100, // 100ms delay for log parsing\n    25\t  CODON_CLEANUP_DELAY_MS: 100, // 100ms delay for codon cleanup\n    26\t  SELF_TEST_TIMEOUT_MS: process.platform === \"win32\" ? 60000 : 30000, // 60s on Windows, 30s elsewhere\n    27\t} as const;\n    28\t\n    29\t/** Maximum allowed shimIdleTimeout in seconds */\n    30\texport const SHIM_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MAX_SECONDS = 600;\n    31\tconst SHIM_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MAX_MINUTES = SHIM_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MAX_SECONDS / 60;\n    32\t\n    33\t/**\n    34\t * Platform-specific retry configuration for directory cleanup.\n    35\t * Windows requires more retries and longer delays due to file locking after process termination.\n    36\t */\n    37\texport const CLEANUP_RETRY_CONFIG = {\n    38\t  windows: {\n    39\t    maxRetries: 10, // More retries for Windows file locking issues\n    40\t    initialDelay: 50, // Start with 50ms, doubles each retry (exponential backoff)\n    41\t  },\n    42\t  default: {\n    43\t    maxRetries: 5, // Standard retries for Unix-like systems\n    44\t    initialDelay: 10, // Start with 10ms\n    45\t  },\n    46\t} as const;\n    47\t\n    48\t/**\n    49\t * Common typos/mistakes mapped to correct field names.\n    50\t * Used to provide helpful \"Did you mean X?\" suggestions.\n    51\t */\n    52\texport const FIELD_TYPO_MAP: Record<string, string> = {\n    53\t  // System prompt typos\n    54\t  systemPromptFile: \"appendSystemPromptFile\",\n    55\t  systemPromptText: \"appendSystemPromptText\",\n    56\t  systemPrompt: \"appendSystemPromptFile or appendSystemPromptText\",\n    57\t\n    58\t  // Prompt typos\n    59\t  prompt: \"promptFile or promptText\",\n    60\t  prompts: \"promptFile\",\n    61\t  promptFiles: \"promptFile\",\n    62\t\n    63\t  // Checkpointing typos\n    64\t  trackedFiles: \"checkpointedFiles\",\n    65\t  tracking: \"checkpointedFiles\",\n    66\t  tracked: \"checkpointedFiles\",\n    67\t  watchedFiles: \"checkpointedFiles\",\n    68\t  fileTracking: \"checkpointedFiles\",\n    69\t\n    70\t  // Rig typos\n    71\t  rig: \"rigSetup\",\n    72\t  setup: \"rigSetup\",\n    73\t  preSetup: \"rigSetup\",\n    74\t\n    75\t  // Archive typos\n    76\t  archiveRigs: \"archiveOnSuccess\",\n    77\t  rigTeardown: \"archiveOnSuccess\",\n    78\t  teardown: \"archiveOnSuccess\",\n    79\t  archive: \"archiveOnSuccess\",\n    80\t  cleanup: \"archiveOnSuccess\",\n    81\t  archiveRig: \"archiveOnSuccess\",\n    82\t  archiving: \"archiveOnSuccess\",\n    83\t  archives: \"archiveOnSuccess\",\n    84\t\n    85\t  // Other typos\n    86\t  environment: \"env\",\n    87\t  envVars: \"env\",\n    88\t  outputs: \"outputFiles\",\n    89\t  output: \"outputFiles\",\n    90\t  continuation: \"continuationMode\",\n    91\t  mode: \"continuationMode\",\n    92\t};\n    93\t\n    94\t// -------------\n    95\t// Error Formatting\n    96\t// -------------\n    97\t\n    98\t/**\n    99\t * Format Zod validation errors into a user-friendly message.\n   100\t * Provides context about which codon has the error and what field is affected.\n   101\t *\n   102\t * Handles both:\n   103\t * - Direct codon array validation (path: [0, \"field\"])\n   104\t * - Hank file validation (path: [\"hank\", 0, \"field\"])\n   105\t */\n   106\tfunction formatZodErrors(error: z.ZodError, rawConfig: unknown): string {\n   107\t  const errors: string[] = [];\n   108\t\n   109\t  for (const issue of error.issues) {\n   110\t    // Clone the path to avoid mutation\n   111\t    let adjustedPath = [...issue.path];\n   112\t    let errorMsg = \"\";\n   113\t\n   114\t    // Handle paths that start with \"hank\" (from hankFileSchema)\n   115\t    // Convert [\"hank\", 0, \"field\"] to [0, \"field\"] and extract the hank array\n   116\t    let hankArray: unknown[] | null = null;\n   117\t    if (adjustedPath[0] === \"hank\") {\n   118\t      const hankFile = rawConfig as { hank?: unknown[] };\n   119\t      if (hankFile?.hank && Array.isArray(hankFile.hank)) {\n   120\t        hankArray = hankFile.hank;\n   121\t      }\n   122\t      adjustedPath = adjustedPath.slice(1); // Remove \"hank\" prefix\n   123\t    } else if (Array.isArray(rawConfig)) {\n   124\t      hankArray = rawConfig;\n   125\t    }\n   126\t\n   127\t    // Determine if this is a codon-level error\n   128\t    if (adjustedPath[0] === undefined && issue.code === \"too_small\") {\n   129\t      errorMsg = `  - ${issue.message}`;\n   130\t    } else if (typeof adjustedPath[0] === \"number\") {\n   131\t      // This is an error in a specific codon/loop\n   132\t      const codonIndex = adjustedPath[0];\n   133\t      const codonData = hankArray ? hankArray[codonIndex] : null;\n   134\t      const codonId = (codonData as Record<string, unknown>)?.id || `index ${codonIndex}`;\n   135\t      const codonName = (codonData as Record<string, unknown>)?.name || \"unnamed\";\n   136\t      const isLoop = (codonData as Record<string, unknown>)?.type === \"loop\";\n   137\t      const itemType = isLoop ? \"Loop\" : \"Codon\";\n   138\t\n   139\t      if (isLoop && adjustedPath[1] === \"codons\" && typeof adjustedPath[2] === \"number\") {\n   140\t        const nestedIndex = adjustedPath[2];\n   141\t        const nestedCodons = (codonData as Record<string, unknown>)?.codons;\n   142\t        const nestedData = Array.isArray(nestedCodons)\n   143\t          ? (nestedCodons[nestedIndex] as Record<string, unknown> | undefined)\n   144\t          : undefined;\n   145\t        const nestedId = nestedData?.id || `index ${nestedIndex}`;\n   146\t        const nestedName = nestedData?.name || \"unnamed\";\n   147\t\n   148\t        if (adjustedPath.length === 3) {\n   149\t          errorMsg = `  - ${itemType} \"${codonName}\" (${codonId}) -> Codon \"${nestedName}\" (${nestedId}): ${issue.message}`;\n   150\t        } else {\n   151\t          const fieldPath = adjustedPath.slice(3).join(\".\");\n   152\t          errorMsg = `  - ${itemType} \"${codonName}\" (${codonId}) -> Codon \"${nestedName}\" (${nestedId}) - ${fieldPath}: ${issue.message}`;\n   153\t        }\n   154\t      } else if (adjustedPath.length === 1) {\n   155\t        // Top-level codon/loop error\n   156\t        errorMsg = `  - ${itemType} \"${codonName}\" (${codonId}): ${issue.message}`;\n   157\t      } else {\n   158\t        // Field-specific error\n   159\t        const fieldPath = adjustedPath.slice(1).join(\".\");\n   160\t        errorMsg = `  - ${itemType} \"${codonName}\" (${codonId}) - ${fieldPath}: ${issue.message}`;\n   161\t      }\n   162\t    } else if (issue.code === \"unrecognized_keys\") {\n   163\t      // Handle unrecognized keys specially\n   164\t      const keys = (issue as z.ZodIssue & { keys?: string[] }).keys?.join(\", \");\n   165\t      const codonIndex = typeof adjustedPath[0] === \"number\" ? adjustedPath[0] : undefined;\n   166\t      const codonData = codonIndex !== undefined && hankArray ? hankArray[codonIndex] : null;\n   167\t      const codonId =\n   168\t        (codonData as Record<string, unknown>)?.id ||\n   169\t        (codonIndex !== undefined ? `index ${codonIndex}` : \"\");\n   170\t      const codonName = (codonData as Record<string, unknown>)?.name || \"unnamed\";\n   171\t\n   172\t      if (codonIndex !== undefined) {\n   173\t        const isLoop = (codonData as Record<string, unknown>)?.type === \"loop\";\n   174\t        const itemType = isLoop ? \"Loop\" : \"Codon\";\n   175\t        const validFields = isLoop ? VALID_LOOP_FIELDS.join(\", \") : VALID_CODON_FIELDS.join(\", \");\n   176\t        errorMsg = `  - ${itemType} \"${codonName}\" (${codonId}) has unrecognized field(s): ${keys}. Fix: Remove these fields or check for typos. Valid fields are: ${validFields}.`;\n   177\t      } else {\n   178\t        // Root-level unrecognized key — check if it's a codon field that was misplaced\n   179\t        const unrecognizedKeys = (issue as z.ZodIssue & { keys?: string[] }).keys || [];\n   180\t        const codonFieldHints = unrecognizedKeys.filter((k) =>\n   181\t          VALID_CODON_FIELDS.includes(k as (typeof VALID_CODON_FIELDS)[number]),\n   182\t        );\n   183\t        if (codonFieldHints.length > 0) {\n   184\t          errorMsg = `  - Unrecognized field(s) at hank root: ${keys}. \"${codonFieldHints.join('\", \"')}\" is a per-codon field — move it inside a codon in the \"hank\" array.`;\n   185\t        } else {\n   186\t          const validRootFields =\n   187\t            \"$schema, meta, overrides, requirements, globalSystemPromptFile, globalSystemPromptText, hank\";\n   188\t          errorMsg = `  - Unrecognized field(s) at hank root: ${keys}. Valid root fields are: ${validRootFields}.`;\n   189\t        }\n   190\t      }\n   191\t    } else {\n   192\t      // Generic error\n   193\t      const fieldPath = issue.path.join(\".\");\n   194\t      errorMsg = `  - ${fieldPath || \"Configuration\"}: ${issue.message}`;\n   195\t    }\n   196\t\n   197\t    errors.push(errorMsg);\n   198\t  }\n   199\t\n   200\t  return errors.join(\"\\n\");\n   201\t}\n   202\t\n   203\t// -------------\n   204\t// Configuration Schema\n   205\t// -------------\n   206\t\n   207\tconst shellCommandWorkingDirectory = [\"project\"] as const;\n   208\t\n   209\t// when running rig setup commands, it's useful to have \"lastCopied\" option\n   210\t// to coordinate with copy commands\n   211\tconst rigSetupCommandWorkingDirectory = [...shellCommandWorkingDirectory, \"lastCopied\"] as const;\n   212\t\n   213\texport const shellCommandSchema = z.object({\n   214\t  type: z.literal(\"command\").describe(\"Type of setup operation\"),\n   215\t  command: z.object({\n   216\t    run: z.string().min(1, \"Command cannot be empty\").describe(\"Shell command to execute\"),\n   217\t    workingDirectory: z\n   218\t      .enum(shellCommandWorkingDirectory)\n   219\t      .optional()\n   220\t      .default(\"project\")\n"}]},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T12:28:32.911Z"}
